WEBVTT

00:05.470 --> 00:06.730
<i>The summer recess.</i>

00:07.350 --> 00:08.920
<i>Also known as summer break.</i>

00:10.110 --> 00:12.640
<i>Most students return to 
their family homes,</i>

00:12.640 --> 00:14.790
<i>but there are a few who stay at school.</i>

00:15.780 --> 00:18.410
<i>Patrick and I are among those who remain.</i>

00:18.920 --> 00:20.790
The tip of your sword is drifting again!

00:28.960 --> 00:31.180
Sorry! I used too much strength.

00:35.640 --> 00:38.640
It's okay. I'm used to it by now.

00:39.970 --> 00:43.850
Sorry to have you spar with me 
every day, even over break.

00:43.850 --> 00:45.820
I'm the one who asked you to do it.

00:45.820 --> 00:48.650
I don't want you sending me 
airborne during class again.

00:48.650 --> 00:51.410
I've been practicing 
controlling my strength.

00:51.410 --> 00:54.640
Using this magic slab meant 
for people at level 60.

00:54.640 --> 00:55.660
What is that?

00:56.040 --> 01:00.160
I'm practicing using just enough 
force on this without bending it.

01:00.850 --> 01:01.290
Oh...

01:04.430 --> 01:06.960
<i>It still goes wrong sometimes.</i>

01:07.310 --> 01:09.120
Is it that brittle?

01:09.120 --> 01:12.970
<i>It was going so well during 
my solo practice sessions...</i>

01:37.300 --> 01:40.870
<b>Villainess Level 99</b>

01:37.670 --> 01:40.870
I May Be the Hidden Boss but I'm Not the Demon Lord

02:45.040 --> 02:47.300
<i>Afternoons are for studying 
on our own in the classroom.</i>

02:47.300 --> 02:49.680
<i>There's nothing to do back 
at the dorms, anyway.</i>

02:50.020 --> 02:51.800
<i>And besides, lately...</i>

02:51.800 --> 02:53.500
M-Miss Yumiella...

02:54.040 --> 02:54.780
Yes?

02:54.780 --> 02:57.280
There's a part of this assignment 
that we don't understand.

02:57.280 --> 02:59.530
Would you mind giving us some advice?

02:59.810 --> 03:01.790
Of course. Which part is it?

03:01.790 --> 03:03.450
Thank you!

03:04.130 --> 03:08.540
<i>People have been approaching me 
more frequently, just like this.</i>

03:08.540 --> 03:10.900
So, um, you and Master Patrick...

03:10.900 --> 03:11.450
Huh?

03:11.450 --> 03:14.300
What is it you two are 
always doing together?

03:14.950 --> 03:16.880
Training to level up.

03:16.880 --> 03:18.040
Huh?

03:18.040 --> 03:22.130
Could it be that you two are 
interested in leveling up, as well?

03:23.340 --> 03:25.280
Just ask me at any time.

03:25.280 --> 03:27.530
I can recommend dungeons for you,

03:27.530 --> 03:30.640
and I can even help by using 
the Monster-Calling Flute.

03:30.950 --> 03:32.520
Oh, no, um...

03:33.080 --> 03:35.680
Why do you always jump straight to that?

03:35.680 --> 03:37.050
You're scaring them!

03:37.050 --> 03:39.590
I was only talking about leveling up.

03:39.590 --> 03:41.780
Watch how people are reacting 
to you before you say that!

03:42.210 --> 03:44.300
<i>How they're reacting, huh?</i>

03:45.250 --> 03:47.450
Master Patrick and Miss Yumiella are like...

03:47.450 --> 03:49.570
A beast tamer and a wild beast.

03:49.570 --> 03:50.790
I can see it!

03:50.790 --> 03:52.290
<i>I can hear you.</i>

03:52.290 --> 03:54.740
But don't they look a 
bit like siblings, too?

03:54.740 --> 03:56.100
I can see it!

03:56.100 --> 04:00.310
<i>I don't think he and I 
are quite that close...</i>

04:04.310 --> 04:06.510
<i>There's something I've realized recently.</i>

04:06.510 --> 04:08.310
<i>Is it possible that my knowledge...</i>

04:08.960 --> 04:10.810
<i>is too biased toward magic?</i>

04:11.450 --> 04:14.860
<i>Watching Patrick made me 
realize the importance</i>

04:15.140 --> 04:17.860
<i>of the techniques involved in combat, 
as well as strategy and leadership.</i>

04:18.250 --> 04:20.820
<i>What I need in order to 
become even stronger is...</i>

04:21.240 --> 04:23.510
<i>Yes! Combat techniques!</i>

04:24.540 --> 04:28.240
<i>Maybe I should just read every 
military-related book I see.</i>

04:30.670 --> 04:32.000
<i>Alicia?!</i>

04:32.510 --> 04:33.590
<i>Is she alone?</i>

04:34.360 --> 04:36.470
<i>Her usual trio is back 
home with their families,</i>

04:36.470 --> 04:38.920
<i>so I guess she's the one 
who's all alone now.</i>

04:42.410 --> 04:43.550
Miss Yumiella.

04:43.870 --> 04:45.640
What is it, Miss Alicia?

04:46.020 --> 04:47.590
I have a favor to ask.

04:47.590 --> 04:48.270
Huh?

04:48.270 --> 04:51.400
Would you please teach me how to use magic?

04:54.480 --> 04:58.510
I see. So you don't understand 
light magic all that well.

04:58.510 --> 04:59.650
Right.

04:59.940 --> 05:02.680
Since light magic is such a rare attribute,

05:02.680 --> 05:06.350
even the teachers seem to be 
unsure how to teach me about it.

05:06.780 --> 05:09.540
There aren't many books about 
it at the castle, either.

05:09.910 --> 05:13.060
I've been trying to find 
something here, but...

05:13.700 --> 05:17.300
If the castle doesn't have any, the 
school library isn't likely to, either.

05:17.970 --> 05:23.350
I've heard that your dark magic is 
just as uncommon as light magic.

05:23.350 --> 05:26.180
I was hoping there might be 
something you could teach me.

05:28.580 --> 05:32.310
All right. If there's anything I 
can help with, I'd be glad to.

05:32.700 --> 05:34.060
Thank you so much!

05:34.400 --> 05:36.070
<i>That heroine smile!</i>

05:36.410 --> 05:37.730
Let's get right to it!

05:37.370 --> 05:41.070
<b>Diligent</b>

05:37.730 --> 05:41.070
How did you learn about your dark magic?

05:41.570 --> 05:44.070
<i>I can't tell her I saw it in the game.</i>

05:44.170 --> 05:53.600
Alicia

05:44.170 --> 05:53.600
Monsters, rest in peace within this light!

05:44.610 --> 05:49.020
<i>Naturally, I know about light 
magic because I played the game.</i>

05:49.020 --> 05:53.710
<i>But it wouldn't make sense for me to 
know things there are no books about.</i>

05:54.180 --> 05:56.070
<i>How do I explain it?</i>

05:57.110 --> 06:00.690
For starters, why don't you try 
envisioning a finishing move?

06:00.690 --> 06:02.110
Something like this.

06:02.720 --> 06:04.140
Finishing...?

06:04.140 --> 06:06.110
<i>Oh, I guess she doesn't 
have a finishing move.</i>

06:06.440 --> 06:12.230
Well, then, do you have any strong 
memories that involve light?

06:12.690 --> 06:14.390
Memories, huh?

06:14.390 --> 06:19.230
Yes. Maybe you could recall them 
when you want to use light magic.

06:19.230 --> 06:20.430
Light...

06:20.920 --> 06:24.860
It reminds me of seeing the starry sky 
with my grandma back in the country.

06:25.150 --> 06:27.370
Stars... I see.

06:27.600 --> 06:29.630
The place where I lived was very rural.

06:29.630 --> 06:33.250
It didn't have tall buildings or anything.

06:33.890 --> 06:39.220
But because of that, the whole sky was 
filled with stars, and it was so beautiful.

06:42.300 --> 06:44.430
When I think about those days,

06:44.430 --> 06:47.920
the thought that I'm here at this 
academy now seems like a dream.

06:49.700 --> 06:51.270
Thanks, Miss Yumiella!

06:51.910 --> 06:55.220
I think this has helped 
me figure something out.

06:55.220 --> 06:58.150
I hope you'll let me come to you 
for advice again if I need it!

06:58.660 --> 07:00.770
Uh, sure. Anytime.

07:00.770 --> 07:02.120
Well, bye, then!

07:18.990 --> 07:20.150
Patrick.

07:20.760 --> 07:23.130
This is from the queen.

07:23.490 --> 07:25.260
You went to the castle?

07:25.540 --> 07:27.210
Well, yeah.

07:27.210 --> 07:30.340
I guess the sons of margraves are 
pretty busy people, huh?

07:30.340 --> 07:31.760
Yeah, pretty much.

07:32.090 --> 07:35.960
These are pastries. Do you want 
to eat them with me in my room?

07:35.960 --> 07:36.790
Wha—

07:36.790 --> 07:41.270
Rita... er, my maid will 
prepare some good tea for us.

07:41.590 --> 07:44.650
Don't invite a man into a lady's 
room like it's no big deal!

07:46.840 --> 07:48.160
I'm sorry.

07:50.160 --> 07:52.160
No... I'm sorry, too.

07:53.230 --> 07:55.230
Why don't we eat in the cafeteria?

07:55.230 --> 07:57.080
Yes, let's.

08:04.890 --> 08:05.910
This is good.

08:05.910 --> 08:06.750
Isn't it?

08:06.750 --> 08:08.850
Why do you sound so proud?

08:09.930 --> 08:12.430
Master Patrick and Miss Yumiella...

08:12.430 --> 08:14.430
They really are close.

08:15.400 --> 08:19.440
<i>Summer break ended, and the season of 
the martial arts competition arrived.</i>

08:19.900 --> 08:24.190
<i>The martial arts competition is 
a schoolwide event consisting of</i>

08:24.710 --> 08:27.510
<i>a sword fighting portion conducted 
in one-on-one tournament format</i>

08:27.510 --> 08:29.700
<i>and an individually scored magic portion.</i>

08:30.350 --> 08:34.890
<i>In the game, Alicia stirs up the 
crowd with her light magic,</i>

08:34.890 --> 08:36.370
<i>but I don't participate.</i>

08:36.920 --> 08:40.180
<i>Powerful nobles come to 
watch this competition,</i>

08:40.180 --> 08:42.570
<i>so it's a chance for students 
striving to be military officers</i>

08:42.570 --> 08:44.210
<i>to show what they can do.</i>

08:44.900 --> 08:47.220
<i>I don't think it'd be right 
to interfere with that.</i>

08:48.670 --> 08:51.510
Ah, the martial arts competition. 
Are you participating?

08:51.510 --> 08:54.010
Of course not. What about you?

08:54.300 --> 08:55.860
I'll pass, too.

08:56.300 --> 08:58.770
I have no interest in joining the military.

08:59.210 --> 09:03.280
Anyway, who would even want the prize 
they're offering the winner this year?

09:03.280 --> 09:04.320
Prize?

09:05.350 --> 09:09.820
The winners in each portion will receive... 
an amulet that enhances dark magic?

09:10.170 --> 09:12.170
Is that a rare item I don't know about?

09:12.600 --> 09:16.390
But you're the only one 
who can use dark magic,

09:16.390 --> 09:19.420
and if you get any stronger 
than you already are...

09:18.710 --> 09:19.420
I want it.

09:19.420 --> 09:19.790
Huh?

09:20.070 --> 09:22.290
I really want it! I want it so bad!

09:22.530 --> 09:24.420
I'm gonna get it, whatever it takes!

09:25.930 --> 09:27.920
Hey! Take it easy, Yumiella!

09:31.200 --> 09:33.040
I'm entering the martial arts competition.

09:33.040 --> 09:34.300
You're scaring me.

09:35.160 --> 09:37.600
If I hadn't learned what the prize was,

09:37.600 --> 09:40.930
the winners would have unknowingly
become targets for robbery.

09:41.560 --> 09:42.940
You're so scary.

09:42.940 --> 09:47.890
So please see that I am entered in 
both portions of the competition.

09:47.890 --> 09:49.190
Sure, sure.

09:49.720 --> 09:54.160
<i>Event rewards must be obtained by 
legitimately winning the event. That's my motto.</i>

09:56.460 --> 09:58.450
<i>I didn't think she'd actually take the bait.</i>

10:02.550 --> 10:06.000
<b>The Hidden Boss Participates in the Martial Arts Competition</b>

10:10.330 --> 10:12.280
This is an even bigger deal 
than I thought it'd be.

10:12.280 --> 10:16.730
I heard that those amulets 
were given to the principal

10:16.730 --> 10:19.600
by the king himself, to 
be passed along to you.

10:20.270 --> 10:24.160
Yet they decided to offer them 
as prizes, which must mean...

10:24.160 --> 10:26.230
The principal set me up.

10:26.610 --> 10:31.340
He's probably trying to use this as a 
chance to show you off to the nobles.

10:31.970 --> 10:37.030
Are these nobles seeing this as a 
trip to a zoo to see the lions

10:37.030 --> 10:40.760
or a viewing of the military's latest weapon?

10:42.050 --> 10:43.750
It's tough being popular.

10:44.330 --> 10:47.030
We will now determine the match-ups 
for the sword fighting portion.

10:47.030 --> 10:48.880
Participants, to the center of the arena.

10:49.140 --> 10:52.130
Well, off I go. I'll do my best.

10:52.450 --> 10:54.050
Yeah, good luck.

10:54.050 --> 10:56.050
Uh, maybe don't do your "best," though!

10:56.050 --> 10:59.880
"Good enough" is good enough!
In fact, do your best to hold back!

10:59.880 --> 11:01.470
<i>He's asking a lot.</i>

11:03.050 --> 11:06.580
<i>The sword fighting match-ups 
are determined by lottery.</i>

11:07.960 --> 11:09.940
<i>Edwin and William...</i>

11:09.940 --> 11:11.940
<i>are both in the left block.</i>

11:18.330 --> 11:20.060
Number three on the right.

11:23.250 --> 11:26.840
I hear you stayed at school all 
through the summer recess.

11:26.840 --> 11:28.250
Huh? Yes...

11:28.470 --> 11:30.820
I spent the whole time training.

11:30.820 --> 11:33.000
Don't think this'll end 
like it did last time.

11:33.650 --> 11:36.010
I'm level 20 now!

11:36.010 --> 11:39.260
<i>I don't know if that's impressive or not...</i>

11:39.790 --> 11:43.000
<i>But I'm curious to know 
what he did to level up.</i>

11:43.550 --> 11:45.760
<i>Take this! The three sacred 
implements of idle chatter!</i>

11:46.160 --> 11:50.520
I see.

11:46.270 --> 11:47.410
I see.

11:47.160 --> 11:50.520
That's amazing.

11:47.410 --> 11:48.640
That's amazing.

11:48.410 --> 11:50.520
Please tell me more.

11:48.640 --> 11:50.520
Please tell me more.

11:50.830 --> 11:52.550
Are you mocking me?

11:52.550 --> 11:54.050
<i>It didn't work.</i>

11:54.400 --> 11:56.730
Look... I'm sorry.

11:56.730 --> 11:57.400
What?

11:57.810 --> 12:02.550
I heard from Captain Adolf 
that you're level 99.

12:03.090 --> 12:05.790
And if he says so, it must be true.

12:06.420 --> 12:08.800
I'm just glad the misunderstanding 
is cleared up.

12:08.800 --> 12:13.420
My dream is to surpass Captain 
Adolf. In other words...

12:13.720 --> 12:16.760
Beating you would bring me 
closer to achieving my dream.

12:17.260 --> 12:19.660
<i>You're actually getting 
closer to your own death.</i>

12:25.250 --> 12:27.480
The winner: Miles Clory!

12:27.760 --> 12:29.840
<i>I'm up next.</i>

12:32.960 --> 12:37.300
Second match: Yumiella 
Dolkness versus Lewis Lexam!

12:42.630 --> 12:44.810
<i>There's no way I'm going to lose,</i>

12:44.810 --> 12:47.910
<i>but he's seeing this as 
a part of job-hunting.</i>

12:48.300 --> 12:50.450
<i>I'll give him a chance to shine.</i>

12:50.770 --> 12:54.900
<i>I need to hold back enough to let 
the audience see his strength.</i>

12:55.310 --> 12:58.350
<i>The only concern is the 
durability of these swords.</i>

12:58.350 --> 13:00.590
<i>A broken weapon is instant disqualification,</i>

13:00.590 --> 13:02.930
<i>so I went to some pains to get this sword.</i>

13:03.620 --> 13:07.680
<i>Most swords snap right in two when 
I use them at full strength.</i>

13:11.690 --> 13:15.150
<i>Okay. That should be enough 
to keep my sword intact.</i>

13:15.970 --> 13:17.210
I withdraw!

13:17.210 --> 13:17.840
Huh?

13:17.840 --> 13:20.150
The winner... is Yumiella Dolkness.

13:21.330 --> 13:23.460
<i>Did he suddenly start to feel ill?</i>

13:24.160 --> 13:27.570
<i>From there, I advanced to the final round...</i>

13:25.420 --> 13:26.640
I withdraw.

13:27.570 --> 13:28.440
I withdraw.

13:28.440 --> 13:30.080
<i>without even having to fight anyone.</i>

13:30.080 --> 13:31.580
I-I withdraw!

13:42.090 --> 13:44.390
The winner: William Ares!

13:44.890 --> 13:46.950
<i>Edwin is a magic swordsman.</i>

13:46.950 --> 13:49.140
<i>When he fights with only a sword,</i>

13:49.140 --> 13:51.560
<i>he's at a disadvantage against William.</i>

13:53.000 --> 13:56.780
The final round: Yumiella 
Dolkness versus William Ares!

13:57.350 --> 14:01.390
I won't withdraw. 
I'm gonna fight you fair and square.

14:01.760 --> 14:04.290
<i>The final round, and I finally get to fight.</i>

14:04.640 --> 14:08.920
<i>Thank goodness. Winning the whole thing by 
default would've left a bad taste in my mouth.</i>

14:10.840 --> 14:12.980
My weapon is the Greatsword of Strodo!

14:12.980 --> 14:15.210
It won't be like that wooden sword!

14:15.540 --> 14:17.480
<i>I remember that from the game.</i>

14:17.480 --> 14:20.770
<i>It's supposed to be a sword you 
get near the end of the story.</i>

14:21.090 --> 14:23.410
<i>How did he get it?</i>

14:24.410 --> 14:25.670
<i>Guess he has connections.</i>

14:27.510 --> 14:29.600
Final round! Begin!

14:39.220 --> 14:40.430
Damn you!

14:40.430 --> 14:42.490
<i>He's already out of breath.</i>

14:42.490 --> 14:45.320
<i>That's what happens when you use 
a weapon that's above your level.</i>

14:46.930 --> 14:48.950
All you're doing is evading.

14:49.240 --> 14:52.560
<i>He's right. Just evading the 
whole time would be boring.</i>

14:52.560 --> 14:55.230
<i>It's the final. I should make it climactic</i>

14:55.230 --> 14:57.960
<i>and contribute to the 
excitement of the event.</i>

14:58.560 --> 15:02.090
<i>If I deflect his attacks like Patrick 
does, I won't have to dodge.</i>

15:07.680 --> 15:09.350
<i>No! It's about to break!</i>

15:09.350 --> 15:11.010
<i>If my sword breaks, I'm disqualified!</i>

15:11.010 --> 15:12.620
<i>Yumiella Punch!</i>

15:14.780 --> 15:15.990
<i>Allow me to explain.</i>

15:15.990 --> 15:20.330
<i>Yumiella Punch is an ultra
high-speed punch that I can use.</i>

15:20.330 --> 15:22.520
<i>People at low levels can't even see it.</i>

15:22.840 --> 15:27.530
My sword... got shattered 
by a dull blade like that?

15:27.810 --> 15:29.530
<i>Good. He didn't notice.</i>

15:29.840 --> 15:32.600
The winner: Yumiella Dolkness!

15:35.170 --> 15:37.410
<i>My hand kind of moved of its own accord,</i>

15:37.410 --> 15:39.650
<i>but I'm glad nobody seemed to notice.</i>

15:40.450 --> 15:42.660
She broke a greatsword with her bare hand?

15:44.610 --> 15:47.270
<i>The latter half of the competition 
is the magic portion.</i>

15:48.170 --> 15:50.300
<i>Participants display their 
magic in order by level,</i>

15:50.300 --> 15:53.810
<i>and they're scored by academy 
teachers and palace mages.</i>

15:54.450 --> 15:57.930
<i>I'm up last, so I have some free time.</i>

15:58.290 --> 16:00.840
Impressive showing in the 
sword fighting portion.

16:02.560 --> 16:03.340
Thank you.

16:03.340 --> 16:05.570
But the magic portion won't be so easy.

16:06.010 --> 16:07.960
You'll be scored not only 
on the strength of your magic,

16:07.960 --> 16:11.570
but on the type you use and 
your accuracy, as well.

16:12.010 --> 16:13.430
My level may be lower,

16:13.430 --> 16:17.210
but since I can use all four major 
elements, I should have an advantage.

16:17.210 --> 16:18.810
<i>Really?</i>

16:19.720 --> 16:22.700
What did you do to level up 
during the summer recess?

16:22.700 --> 16:27.520
I didn't go into dungeons alone 
or use a Monster-Calling Flute.

16:27.520 --> 16:28.840
I did it the right way.

16:29.130 --> 16:30.240
<i>The right way?</i>

16:30.590 --> 16:32.870
There's one thing I wanted to tell you.

16:32.870 --> 16:33.850
What is it?

16:34.170 --> 16:37.680
I guess it's really true 
that you're level 99.

16:38.210 --> 16:40.230
I apologize for doubting you.

16:41.000 --> 16:43.270
I'm just glad the misunderstanding 
is cleared up.

16:43.270 --> 16:44.890
But I'm sorry to say...

16:44.890 --> 16:47.610
it doesn't change the fact 
that I'll never like you.

16:48.090 --> 16:51.080
I'm going to be the top 
mage in this kingdom,

16:51.440 --> 16:56.240
and as the first step toward achieving 
that, I'm going to win this competition.

16:56.940 --> 16:59.370
I'll be applying my full strength, as well.

16:59.610 --> 17:01.840
Just the way I want it. Goodbye.

17:03.660 --> 17:06.380
First-year, Alicia Ehnleit.

17:15.430 --> 17:16.730
Sun Rain!

17:25.900 --> 17:27.340
<i>This is...</i>

17:28.300 --> 17:31.400
It reminds me of seeing the 
starry sky with my grandma...

17:31.850 --> 17:34.480
<i>The same magic she used in the game.</i>

17:34.970 --> 17:36.760
<i>See? You can do it if you try.</i>

17:37.690 --> 17:42.040
<i>I guess that's to be expected. 
She's the heroine, after all.</i>

17:42.780 --> 17:46.550
<i>It's only natural that things would 
go just the way they did in the game.</i>

17:49.610 --> 17:52.130
Alicia Ehnleit: 88 points!

17:52.590 --> 17:55.550
I never knew I could do that...

17:55.870 --> 17:59.290
Above all, the rarity of her light magic

17:59.290 --> 18:02.810
and the beauty of her spell 
were the key to her score.

18:03.250 --> 18:07.710
<i>If rarity counts, 
I might have a chance, too.</i>

18:15.680 --> 18:21.050
<i>In magic alone, he might win 
in the same way William did.</i>

18:23.210 --> 18:25.540
Edwin Valschein: 90 points!

18:27.110 --> 18:29.770
First-year, Oswald Grimsarde.

18:44.260 --> 18:45.400
Oh, my!

18:55.210 --> 18:56.910
<i>He has not only accuracy,</i>

18:56.910 --> 18:59.580
<i>but also a combination
of multiple types of magic.</i>

18:59.950 --> 19:03.040
<i>He was right. He's a genius.</i>

19:12.650 --> 19:14.920
Oswald Grimsarde: 100 points!

19:15.870 --> 19:17.740
Remarkable! A perfect score!

19:18.350 --> 19:19.410
<i>A perfect score?</i>

19:24.360 --> 19:28.670
I've won. You can't beat 100 
points, no matter what you do.

19:28.670 --> 19:32.440
But if I get 100 points, it'll be a draw.

19:34.460 --> 19:39.530
<i>So I said, but I haven't decided 
which spell to use yet.</i>

19:40.040 --> 19:41.700
The final competitor:

19:41.700 --> 19:44.420
first-year, Yumiella Dolkness!

19:46.800 --> 19:47.710
<i>Patrick?</i>

19:48.370 --> 19:50.570
<i>Why is he so far away?</i>

19:51.270 --> 19:54.320
<i>It's my turn, and he's not in the front row?</i>

19:54.670 --> 19:56.220
<i>Oh, well.</i>

19:56.700 --> 20:00.180
<i>Just watch. I'll do my best 
so you can see it from there.</i>

20:03.400 --> 20:04.980
<i>Why did he back away?</i>

20:07.860 --> 20:10.030
<i>I'm not confident in my control,</i>

20:10.530 --> 20:13.110
<i>so I'll have to go with a display of power.</i>

20:13.920 --> 20:17.870
<i>Take a good look at the power of level 99!</i>

20:19.060 --> 20:20.490
Black Hole!

20:32.630 --> 20:37.760
<i>Ah... How long has it been since 
I cast a spell at full strength?</i>

20:42.190 --> 20:42.940
<i>Oh...</i>

20:46.640 --> 20:50.900
<i>I had no idea I could use 
such beautiful magic, too...</i>

20:58.390 --> 21:02.910
<i>I forgot that this spell always 
causes a miniature typhoon.</i>

21:02.910 --> 21:03.930
We're doomed!

21:03.930 --> 21:04.840
We're all gonna die!

21:04.840 --> 21:06.790
She really is the Demon Lord!

21:07.070 --> 21:09.880
<i>Shoot! I've only used one spell so far!</i>

21:09.880 --> 21:12.790
<i>I need to rack up points with variety!</i>

21:13.280 --> 21:17.300
<i>Dark Bind? Or maybe a healing 
spell like Turbid Flow?</i>

21:17.540 --> 21:19.690
That's it! Stop! We're done!

21:20.360 --> 21:24.950
Wait, please! Save the scoring until 
after you've seen one more spell!

21:24.950 --> 21:25.970
300 points!

21:25.970 --> 21:26.680
Huh?

21:28.170 --> 21:30.310
Isn't 100 points a perfect score?

21:30.520 --> 21:33.780
Don't worry about that! You can 
have 300 points! Just stop this!

21:33.780 --> 21:34.980
You win!

21:38.290 --> 21:40.650
Congratulations on your 
victory, Miss Yumiella.

21:42.790 --> 21:44.120
Thank you.

21:44.610 --> 21:47.120
Now my magic will be stronger.

21:47.840 --> 21:49.620
Is that really necessary, though?

21:50.000 --> 21:53.730
<i>There are too many people in this world 
who don't understand the value of things.</i>

21:55.650 --> 21:57.870
<i>But Patrick will...</i>

21:59.090 --> 22:01.630
Do you really even need that amulet?

22:02.270 --> 22:05.270
<i>Maybe I should show him how much stronger 
this amulet makes my dark magic,</i>

22:05.270 --> 22:07.340
<i>right here and now.</i>

22:07.340 --> 22:08.930
Huh? What's wrong?!
